cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, please cite the manuscript and this archive."
title: "MERGE-benchmark: data and code for benchmarking genomic foundation and sequence-to-function models for variant pathogenicity prediction"
abstract: >-
  Data and code for benchmarking DNA language, evolutionary, protein and
  sequence-to-function models on four variant classes (coding missense, splicing and
  noncoding SNVs, and short non-SNVs) under fixed chromosome-held-out folds, and for
  MERGE (Model Ensemble for Ranking Genomic Effects), which integrates fixed
  model-derived features.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/TheFangLab/MERGE-benchmark"
url: "https://merge.fanglab.cn"
version: "1.0.0"
keywords:
  - variant effect prediction
  - genomic foundation models
  - sequence-to-function models
  - benchmarking
  - ensemble learning
